# Everything in this project is tracked deliberately -- caches, generated
# outputs, run logs, data dumps and all. The only exclusions are the two
# things that cannot or must not go into git:

# Virtualenv: macOS-arm64 binaries, rebuildable with `pip install -r
# requirements.txt`, and contains individual files over GitHub's 100MB
# hard limit. Rebuild it on the new machine rather than carrying it.
.venv/
.venv.broken-stale-path.bak/

# Live API keys and OAuth secrets. Regenerate these from the provider console
# on the new machine; never in git history, where they are permanent.
#
# token.json holds a Google refresh_token + client_secret, and both
# credentials.json files hold an OAuth client secret. CLAUDE.md already
# described these as gitignored, but they were not actually listed here --
# combined with the `git add .` that section 8 of HANDOFF.md used to
# recommend, one routine deploy would have published them.
.env
credentials.json
token.json
.claude/credentials.json
